# LCV-174 AC 7 — polylines and polygons, open and closed: one line per pair
# of distinct consecutive points, and a polygon's closing line only when its
# last point is not its first. World y = 100 - svg y.
bed 100 100
# Every stroke is red and no layer is declared, so one `#ff0000` layer.
layer "#ff0000" #ff0000 output=1 current=1
# An open polyline; the repeated (30, 10) adds nothing.
line 0 10 90 30 90
line 0 30 90 30 70
# A polyline that returns to its start is still just its lines.
line 0 50 90 70 90
line 0 70 90 70 70
line 0 70 70 50 90
# An open polygon, glued sign and exponent, moved down 20: three points
# (10, 70), (30, 70), (20, 20) in svg space, plus the closing line.
line 0 10 30 30 30
line 0 30 30 20 80
line 0 20 80 10 30
# A polygon whose last point is its first: no extra closing line.
line 0 50 50 70 50
line 0 70 50 70 30
line 0 70 30 50 50
